# Contributing to E-Commerce Application

Thank you for your interest in contributing to this project! This document provides guidelines and instructions for contributing.

## Code of Conduct

- Be respectful and inclusive
- Provide constructive feedback
- Help others and share knowledge
- Report inappropriate behavior to maintainers

## Development Environment Setup

### Prerequisites
- Java 17+
- Maven 3.6+
- Git
- An IDE (IntelliJ IDEA, Eclipse, or VS Code)

### Setup Steps
```bash
# 1. Fork the repository on GitHub
# 2. Clone your fork locally
git clone https://github.com/YOUR-USERNAME/agile-project.git
cd agile-project

# 3. Add upstream remote
git remote add upstream https://github.com/ORIGINAL-OWNER/agile-project.git

# 4. Create and checkout develop branch
git checkout develop

# 5. Install dependencies
mvn clean install

# 6. Run the application
mvn spring-boot:run
```

## Workflow for Contributors

### 1. Create a Feature Branch
```bash
git checkout develop
git pull upstream develop
git checkout -b feature/your-feature-name
```

### 2. Make Your Changes
- Follow the existing code style
- Write clean, readable code
- Add comments for complex logic
- Keep commits focused and atomic

### 3. Commit Your Changes
```bash
git add .
git commit -m "type: brief description

Detailed explanation of changes:
- Point 1
- Point 2
- Point 3"
```

**Commit Types:**
- `feat`: New feature
- `fix`: Bug fix
- `docs`: Documentation
- `style`: Code style changes
- `refactor`: Code refactoring
- `test`: Adding tests
- `chore`: Maintenance

### 4. Push and Create Pull Request
```bash
git push origin feature/your-feature-name
```

Then create a Pull Request on GitHub with:
- Clear title and description
- Reference to related issues
- List of changes
- Testing information

### 5. Code Review Process
- Address reviewer comments
- Push additional commits for changes
- Don't force-push after review starts (unless requested)
- Merge only after approval

## Testing

Before submitting a PR, ensure:
```bash
# Run tests
mvn test

# Build the project
mvn clean install

# Check for warnings
mvn clean compile
```

## Code Style Guidelines

### Java Conventions
- Use meaningful variable and method names
- Keep methods small and focused
- Add JavaDoc for public methods
- Follow Google Java Style Guide

### Example:
```java
/**
 * Retrieves a product by its ID
 * 
 * @param id the product ID
 * @return Optional containing the product if found
 */
public Optional<Product> getProductById(Long id) {
    return productRepository.findById(id);
}
```

## Pull Request Guidelines

### Before Submitting:
- [ ] Code is clean and follows style guide
- [ ] Tests pass: `mvn test`
- [ ] Project builds: `mvn clean install`
- [ ] Branch is up to date with develop
- [ ] Commit history is clean
- [ ] PR has descriptive title and description

### PR Title Format:
```
type(scope): brief description

Example:
feat(products): add product search by category
fix(orders): resolve order status update issue
```

### PR Description Template:
```markdown
## Description
Brief overview of changes

## Type of Change
- [ ] Bug fix
- [ ] New feature
- [ ] Breaking change
- [ ] Documentation update

## Related Issues
Closes #(issue number)

## Changes Made
- Change 1
- Change 2
- Change 3

## Testing Performed
- Test 1
- Test 2

## Checklist
- [ ] Code follows style guidelines
- [ ] Self-review completed
- [ ] Tests added/updated
- [ ] Documentation updated
- [ ] No new warnings generated
```

## Reporting Issues

### Bug Report Template:
```markdown
## Description
Clear description of the bug

## Steps to Reproduce
1. Step 1
2. Step 2
3. Step 3

## Expected Behavior
What should happen

## Actual Behavior
What actually happens

## Environment
- Java version
- Maven version
- OS
- Browser (if applicable)

## Logs
Include relevant error messages or logs
```

### Feature Request Template:
```markdown
## Description
Clear description of the requested feature

## Use Case
Why is this feature needed?

## Proposed Solution
How should it work?

## Alternative Solutions
Any alternatives considered?

## Additional Context
Screenshots, mockups, etc.
```

## Getting Help

- Check existing issues and PRs
- Review the documentation
- Ask in GitHub Discussions
- Open an issue with questions

## Recognition

Contributors will be:
- Added to CONTRIBUTORS.md
- Mentioned in release notes
- Given credit for their work

## License

By contributing, you agree that your contributions will be licensed under the MIT License.

---

Thank you for contributing! 🎉
