```

## File Descriptions

### Root Configuration Files

| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `pom.xml` | Maven build configuration with Spring Boot dependencies |
| `.gitignore` | Specifies files/folders Git should ignore |
| `LICENSE` | MIT License for the project |

### Documentation Files

| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `README.md` | Comprehensive project overview and GitHub workflow guide |
| `CONTRIBUTING.md` | Guidelines for contributors and code standards |
| `DEVELOPMENT.md` | Development setup and workflow instructions |
| `API_DOCUMENTATION.md` | Complete REST API endpoint documentation |
| `PROJECT_STRUCTURE.md` | This file describing project structure |

### Source Code Structure

#### Controllers (`src/main/java/.../controller/`)
REST API endpoints for HTTP requests/responses
- `ProductController.java` - CRUD operations for products
- `OrderController.java` - CRUD operations for orders

#### Services (`src/main/java/.../service/`)
Business logic layer
- `ProductService.java` - Product business operations
- `OrderService.java` - Order business operations

#### Models (`src/main/java/.../model/`)
JPA Entity classes
- `Product.java` - Product data model with fields and annotations
- `Order.java` - Order data model with fields and annotations

#### Repositories (`src/main/java/.../repository/`)
Data Access Objects (DAO)
- `ProductRepository.java` - Database operations for products
- `OrderRepository.java` - Database operations for orders

#### Application Entry Point
- `ECommerceApplication.java` - Spring Boot application starter class

### Configuration
- `application.properties` - Database, server, and logging configuration

### Tests
- `ProductServiceTest.java` - Unit tests for ProductService

### CI/CD Configuration
- `.github/workflows/build.yml` - GitHub Actions workflow for automated builds
- `.github/pull_request_template.md` - Standard PR template

## Technology Stack

| Layer | Technology |
|-------|-----------|
| Framework | Spring Boot 3.1.5 |
| Language | Java 17 |
| Database | H2 (in-memory) |
| ORM | Hibernate/JPA |
| Build Tool | Maven |
| Testing | JUnit 5 + Mockito |
| Additional | Lombok (removed due to compilation) |

## Key Features

✅ **RESTful API Design**
- Product CRUD operations
- Order management system
- Search and filter capabilities

✅ **Layered Architecture**
- Controller layer for HTTP handling
- Service layer for business logic
- Repository layer for data access

✅ **Database Integration**
- H2 in-memory database
- JPA annotations for entity mapping
- Repository pattern implementation

✅ **Testing**
- Unit tests with Mockito
- Service layer testing examples

✅ **Documentation**
- Comprehensive API documentation
- Development guides
- Contribution guidelines
- GitHub workflow examples

✅ **CI/CD Ready**
- GitHub Actions workflow
- Automated builds
- Test automation

## Getting Started Quick Reference

```bash
# 1. Clone the repository
git clone https://github.com/yourorg/agile-project.git
cd agile-project

# 2. Build the project
mvn clean install

# 3. Run the application
mvn spring-boot:run

# 4. Access the API
curl http://localhost:8080/api/products

# 5. Access H2 Console
http://localhost:8080/h2-console
```

## Common Development Tasks

### Adding a New Entity
1. Create model in `model/` directory
2. Create repository in `repository/` directory
3. Create service in `service/` directory
4. Create controller in `controller/` directory
5. Add unit tests in `test/` directory

### Making a Contribution
1. Create feature branch: `git checkout -b feature/your-feature`
2. Make changes to files
3. Run tests: `mvn test`
4. Commit: `git commit -m "feat: description"`
5. Push: `git push origin feature/your-feature`
6. Create Pull Request on GitHub

### Building and Testing
```bash
mvn clean install          # Full build
mvn test                   # Run tests
mvn spring-boot:run        # Run application
mvn dependency:tree        # View dependencies
```

## API Endpoints Overview

### Product Endpoints
- `GET /api/products` - List all products
- `GET /api/products/{id}` - Get product by ID
- `POST /api/products` - Create new product
- `PUT /api/products/{id}` - Update product
- `DELETE /api/products/{id}` - Delete product
- `GET /api/products/search/category/{category}` - Search by category
- `GET /api/products/search/name/{name}` - Search by name

### Order Endpoints
- `GET /api/orders` - List all orders
- `GET /api/orders/{id}` - Get order by ID
- `POST /api/orders` - Create new order
- `PUT /api/orders/{id}/status` - Update order status
- `DELETE /api/orders/{id}` - Delete order
- `GET /api/orders/search/customer/{email}` - Search by customer email
- `GET /api/orders/search/status/{status}` - Search by status

## Database Schema

### Products Table
- `id` (Primary Key)
- `name` (Required)
- `description`
- `price` (Required)
- `quantity` (Required)
- `category`

### Orders Table
- `id` (Primary Key)
- `customer_name` (Required)
- `customer_email` (Required)
- `total_amount` (Required)
- `status` (Enum: PENDING, CONFIRMED, SHIPPED, DELIVERED, CANCELLED)
- `created_at` (Auto-populated)
- `updated_at` (Auto-populated)

