# Quick Start Guide

## 🚀 Get Started in 5 Minutes

### Prerequisites
- Java 17+
- Maven 3.6+
- Git

### Step 1: Clone the Repository
```bash
git clone https://github.com/yourorg/agile-project.git
cd agile-project
```

### Step 2: Build the Project
```bash
mvn clean install
```

### Step 3: Run the Application
```bash
mvn spring-boot:run
```

The application starts on `http://localhost:8080`

### Step 4: Test the API

#### Get all products
```bash
curl http://localhost:8080/api/products
```

#### Create a new product
```bash
curl -X POST http://localhost:8080/api/products \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "name": "Laptop",
    "description": "High-performance laptop",
    "price": 999.99,
    "quantity": 10,
    "category": "Electronics"
  }'
```

#### Get all orders
```bash
curl http://localhost:8080/api/orders
```

#### Create a new order
```bash
curl -X POST http://localhost:8080/api/orders \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "customerName": "John Doe",
    "customerEmail": "john@example.com",
    "totalAmount": 1029.98
  }'
```

### Step 5: Access Database Console (Optional)
Navigate to: `http://localhost:8080/h2-console`
- URL: `jdbc:h2:mem:ecommercedb`
- Username: `sa`
- Password: (leave blank)

## 📚 Documentation

| Document | Purpose |
|----------|---------|
| `README.md` | Project overview & GitHub workflow guide |
| `API_DOCUMENTATION.md` | Detailed API reference |
| `DEVELOPMENT.md` | Development setup & workflow |
| `CONTRIBUTING.md` | Contribution guidelines |
| `PROJECT_STRUCTURE.md` | Project architecture overview |

## 🔄 GitHub Workflow

### Create a Feature Branch
```bash
git checkout develop
git pull origin develop
git checkout -b feature/your-feature-name
```

### Make Changes
Edit files and test locally

### Commit Your Changes
```bash
git add .
git commit -m "feat: your feature description"
```

### Push to Remote
```bash
git push origin feature/your-feature-name
```

### Create Pull Request
1. Go to GitHub
2. Click "New pull request"
3. Add description
4. Request reviewers
5. Submit

## 📝 Common Commands

### Build & Run
```bash
mvn clean install              # Full build
mvn spring-boot:run            # Run application
mvn test                       # Run tests
mvn clean package              # Create JAR
```

### Git Workflow
```bash
git status                     # Check status
git add .                      # Stage changes
git commit -m "message"        # Commit
git push origin branch-name    # Push
git pull origin develop        # Pull latest
git log --oneline              # View history
```

### Database Console
Access H2 console: `http://localhost:8080/h2-console`

## 🐛 Troubleshooting

### Build fails?
```bash
mvn clean install -U
```

### Port 8080 in use?
Edit `application.properties`:
```properties
server.port=8081
```

### Tests failing?
```bash
mvn test -Dtest=ProductServiceTest
```

## 📞 Need Help?

1. Check the full `README.md`
2. Review `API_DOCUMENTATION.md` for endpoints
3. See `DEVELOPMENT.md` for detailed guide
4. Open an issue on GitHub
5. Check existing issues/discussions

## ✅ Checklist Before Making PR

- [ ] Code compiles without errors
- [ ] Tests pass: `mvn test`
- [ ] Branch is up to date: `git pull origin develop`
- [ ] Changes are committed: `git add . && git commit -m "message"`
- [ ] Branch is pushed: `git push origin feature/branch`
- [ ] PR description is complete
- [ ] No merge conflicts
- [ ] Code follows style guide

## 🎯 Next Steps

1. ✅ Set up development environment
2. ✅ Run the application
3. ✅ Test the API endpoints
4. ✅ Create a feature branch
5. ✅ Make your first contribution!

