================================================================================
                E-COMMERCE SPRING BOOT PROJECT
         GitHub Development Demonstration Application
================================================================================

PROJECT CREATION DATE: May 3, 2026

================================================================================
PROJECT OVERVIEW
================================================================================

This is a complete, production-ready Spring Boot e-commerce application created
as a demonstration of modern GitHub workflows in development teams.

Key Features:
✅ RESTful API Architecture
✅ Spring Boot 3.1.5 with Java 17
✅ H2 In-Memory Database with JPA/Hibernate
✅ Layered Architecture (Controller → Service → Repository)
✅ Complete API Documentation
✅ GitHub Actions CI/CD Pipeline
✅ Comprehensive Development Guides
✅ Unit Testing with JUnit 5 & Mockito

================================================================================
PROJECT STRUCTURE SUMMARY
================================================================================

📁 Core Application Files (9 Java Classes)
  ├── ECommerceApplication.java (Entry Point)
  ├── Controllers (2)
  │   ├── ProductController.java
  │   └── OrderController.java
  ├── Services (2)
  │   ├── ProductService.java
  │   └── OrderService.java
  ├── Models (2)
  │   ├── Product.java
  │   └── Order.java
  └── Repositories (2)
      ├── ProductRepository.java
      └── OrderRepository.java

📁 Configuration Files (4)
  ├── pom.xml (Maven)
  ├── application.properties (Spring)
  ├── .gitignore (Git)
  └── .github/workflows/build.yml (CI/CD)

📁 Documentation Files (8)
  ├── README.md (Main Documentation + GitHub Guide)
  ├── QUICK_START.md (5-minute Setup)
  ├── API_DOCUMENTATION.md (Complete API Reference)
  ├── DEVELOPMENT.md (Development Guide)
  ├── CONTRIBUTING.md (Contribution Guidelines)
  ├── PROJECT_STRUCTURE.md (Architecture Overview)
  ├── .github/pull_request_template.md (PR Template)
  └── .github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/* (Issue Templates)

📁 License & Testing (2)
  ├── LICENSE (MIT)
  └── ProductServiceTest.java (Unit Tests)

================================================================================
API ENDPOINTS
================================================================================

PRODUCTS:
  GET    /api/products                           List all products
  GET    /api/products/{id}                      Get product by ID
  POST   /api/products                           Create product
  PUT    /api/products/{id}                      Update product
  DELETE /api/products/{id}                      Delete product
  GET    /api/products/search/category/{cat}    Search by category
  GET    /api/products/search/name/{name}       Search by name

ORDERS:
  GET    /api/orders                             List all orders
  GET    /api/orders/{id}                        Get order by ID
  POST   /api/orders                             Create order
  PUT    /api/orders/{id}/status                Update order status
  DELETE /api/orders/{id}                        Delete order
  GET    /api/orders/search/customer/{email}    Search by customer
  GET    /api/orders/search/status/{status}     Search by status

================================================================================
QUICK START
================================================================================

1. BUILD:
   $ mvn clean install

2. RUN:
   $ mvn spring-boot:run

3. TEST:
   $ curl http://localhost:8080/api/products

4. CONSOLE:
   http://localhost:8080/h2-console
   (URL: jdbc:h2:mem:ecommercedb, User: sa, Password: blank)

================================================================================
GITHUB WORKFLOW DOCUMENTATION
================================================================================

This project includes comprehensive GitHub workflow documentation covering:

✅ Git Basics (configuration, cloning, status)
✅ Branching Strategy (Git Flow with feature/bugfix/hotfix branches)
✅ Pull Request Process (creation, review, merge)
✅ Commit Conventions (feat, fix, docs, style, refactor, test)
✅ Merge Conflict Resolution
✅ Best Practices & Anti-patterns
✅ Advanced Git Scenarios (cherry-pick, rebase, squash)
✅ Git Commands Cheat Sheet

👉 See README.md for complete GitHub workflow guide!

================================================================================
TECHNOLOGY STACK
================================================================================

Framework:      Spring Boot 3.1.5
Language:       Java 17
Build Tool:     Maven 3.6+
Database:       H2 (In-Memory)
ORM:            Hibernate/JPA
Testing:        JUnit 5 + Mockito
CI/CD:          GitHub Actions
Version Control: Git

